1
00:00:27,193 --> 00:00:29,095
‎That's right, yesterday…

2
00:00:29,596 --> 00:00:30,897
Hey!

3
00:00:36,569 --> 00:00:40,340
That's right, yesterday… Mariko and I kis…

4
00:00:42,776 --> 00:00:44,010
Kissed…

5
00:01:04,964 --> 00:01:08,234
Huh? What is it?

6
00:01:08,802 --> 00:01:12,439
I'm kind of dizzy, I think…

7
00:01:13,873 --> 00:01:16,943
What? Are you okay?

8
00:01:19,312 --> 00:01:21,081
That was the worst.

9
00:01:34,027 --> 00:01:34,928
Was it a dream?

10
00:01:38,164 --> 00:01:41,000
Part of me wants it to be a dream,
but part of me doesn’t.

11
00:01:53,279 --> 00:01:54,280
Wha-!?

12
00:01:56,249 --> 00:01:59,652
What is it? You're so loud…

13
00:02:06,292 --> 00:02:07,627
I fell asleep, sorry.

14
00:02:07,694 --> 00:02:10,029
You fell asleep? "Sorry"?

15
00:02:10,897 --> 00:02:15,101
I thought I needed to really
hear everything from you.

16
00:02:15,168 --> 00:02:19,038
I didn't know whether to wait for you
to wake up or come back later, and I just…

17
00:02:19,105 --> 00:02:20,540
-I'm sorry.
-Ah, no.

18
00:02:29,115 --> 00:02:32,418
Please tell me everything.

19
00:02:32,485 --> 00:02:34,787
Everything you’ve been doing
without me knowing until now.

20
00:02:34,854 --> 00:02:36,122
In full detail.

21
00:02:39,392 --> 00:02:40,226
‎Okay.

22
00:02:57,510 --> 00:03:02,315
So, the first time I met you

23
00:03:03,149 --> 00:03:04,584
was when I was seven years old.

24
00:03:06,486 --> 00:03:08,955
It was one week
before that kidnapping incident.

25
00:03:11,391 --> 00:03:13,893
On my way home from school, a classmate…

26
00:03:15,962 --> 00:03:19,532
I confessed everything to Mariko.

27
00:03:20,200 --> 00:03:21,501
Every single thing I knew,

28
00:03:21,568 --> 00:03:23,269
-bare and laid out.
-Somebody help!

29
00:03:23,336 --> 00:03:25,638
I felt a self-imposed sense of duty
that I had to protect

30
00:03:26,906 --> 00:03:29,075
you from then on.

31
00:03:29,142 --> 00:03:32,078
Having Mariko listen to the story
of my life could have been

32
00:03:33,112 --> 00:03:37,283
a joyful event, and yet…

33
00:03:39,619 --> 00:03:41,588
because of everything
I’ve done up until now…

34
00:03:44,324 --> 00:03:47,126
it felt like a confession
before receiving a death sentence.

35
00:03:47,193 --> 00:03:50,263
I thought I had to get Tateiwa
to step down from the project,

36
00:03:50,330 --> 00:03:52,699
so I obtained evidence of his misconduct
and went to meet him.

37
00:03:52,765 --> 00:03:53,866
I was like

38
00:03:53,933 --> 00:03:55,969
a criminal climbing the gallows.

39
00:03:56,035 --> 00:03:56,970
Creepy!

40
00:03:57,036 --> 00:03:59,172
-I told you, I won't forgive you.
-Or like

41
00:03:59,239 --> 00:04:03,276
a low-ranking samurai who was ordered
to commit seppuku, but had no subordinate.

42
00:04:04,177 --> 00:04:06,312
Feeling like my stomach was bleeding out,

43
00:04:07,113 --> 00:04:09,415
unable to die.

44
00:04:14,187 --> 00:04:17,523
Even so, talking was
my only way to survive.

45
00:04:19,025 --> 00:04:21,594
So I kept talking.

46
00:04:27,400 --> 00:04:32,472
That's everything.

47
00:04:33,940 --> 00:04:34,774
I'm sorry.

48
00:04:39,779 --> 00:04:40,613
I understand.

49
00:04:42,181 --> 00:04:44,317
I also don’t get it at all.

50
00:04:44,951 --> 00:04:45,818
What?

51
00:04:45,885 --> 00:04:47,253
I’m going to tell you clearly.

52
00:04:48,321 --> 00:04:51,924
First of all, knowing where my home is

53
00:04:52,425 --> 00:04:54,994
and passing in front of it
isn’t something I consider stalking.

54
00:04:55,762 --> 00:04:59,632
When you’re a child, it’s actually quite
common to know where your classmates live

55
00:04:59,699 --> 00:05:04,203
and think, "Ah, that’s her house"
when passing by,

56
00:05:04,270 --> 00:05:05,905
so it isn’t strange at all.

57
00:05:06,806 --> 00:05:08,041
-Thank you.
-However,

58
00:05:09,008 --> 00:05:12,011
coming to the front of my home
specifically to check on

59
00:05:12,078 --> 00:05:14,580
or monitor my actions,

60
00:05:15,348 --> 00:05:18,451
waiting in ambush, or interacting with me
while pretending it's a coincidence,

61
00:05:18,518 --> 00:05:22,155
I feel that kind of behavior
is unacceptable.

62
00:05:24,357 --> 00:05:27,794
-Yes.
-And if you knew I would dislike it,

63
00:05:27,860 --> 00:05:30,763
and you still continued these actions,
that would be, needless to say,

64
00:05:31,397 --> 00:05:33,866
completely unacceptable.
It’s out of the question.

65
00:05:39,505 --> 00:05:40,473
But

66
00:05:41,674 --> 00:05:44,744
I don’t think you would
do something like that.

67
00:05:46,045 --> 00:05:48,548
Because I know you.

68
00:05:50,350 --> 00:05:53,453
In other words, if I had found out
about all these actions

69
00:05:53,519 --> 00:05:55,555
back when I didn’t know you,

70
00:05:56,289 --> 00:05:59,459
I likely would have felt terrified of you.

71
00:06:00,860 --> 00:06:02,762
Even if it was the exact same you.

72
00:06:03,896 --> 00:06:04,764
Yes.

73
00:06:05,965 --> 00:06:06,799
But

74
00:06:07,633 --> 00:06:10,436
now I understand why you were suspected

75
00:06:11,437 --> 00:06:13,773
in Tateiwa and Sayuri's cases.

76
00:06:18,444 --> 00:06:20,847
The incidents are happening all around me.

77
00:06:32,458 --> 00:06:33,626
I’ve decided.

78
00:06:35,128 --> 00:06:37,563
To make sure you don’t do
anything dangerous anymore,

79
00:06:37,630 --> 00:06:40,133
I’m going to stay here
and monitor you for a while.

80
00:06:40,199 --> 00:06:43,636
What? You'll monitor me here?

81
00:06:43,703 --> 00:06:47,240
Besides, Hatano hasn’t been
caught yet, so it’s dangerous, right?

82
00:06:48,107 --> 00:06:51,144
I’m going to live here for a while.

83
00:06:52,278 --> 00:06:53,146
What?

84
00:06:54,514 --> 00:06:55,448
What?

85
00:06:57,784 --> 00:06:58,785
What?

86
00:07:03,423 --> 00:07:06,826
Yesterday, a female office worker
was attacked on her way home,

87
00:07:06,893 --> 00:07:09,328
kidnapped, and held against her will.

88
00:07:09,896 --> 00:07:13,433
The woman was safely
rescued by the police,

89
00:07:13,499 --> 00:07:15,735
but the perpetrator is on the run,

90
00:07:15,802 --> 00:07:18,805
and police continue to search for him.

91
00:07:18,871 --> 00:07:21,908
The suspect on the run
is Satoru Hatano, age 60.

92
00:07:23,009 --> 00:07:25,344
He's still on the run.

93
00:07:26,813 --> 00:07:28,948
What on earth is going on?

94
00:07:30,817 --> 00:07:34,053
Sometimes, Mariko acts in way
I don't understand.

95
00:07:35,455 --> 00:07:37,523
Just like that day, in the summer
of seventh grade.

96
00:07:39,192 --> 00:07:40,026
No,

97
00:07:40,526 --> 00:07:43,329
what happened that summer
doesn't matter right now.

98
00:07:43,396 --> 00:07:44,297
Um…

99
00:07:45,832 --> 00:07:47,867
You don't need to force yourself
to watch that.

100
00:07:48,434 --> 00:07:49,735
What are you talking about?

101
00:07:49,802 --> 00:07:52,004
We have to keep track
of the enemy’s moves.

102
00:07:55,174 --> 00:07:56,742
-Ah, hey.
-Yes?

103
00:07:56,809 --> 00:07:59,946
Uh, is it okay if I sleep right here?

104
00:08:00,012 --> 00:08:02,148
Oh, please use the bed.
I’ll sleep on the sofa.

105
00:08:02,215 --> 00:08:04,350
No, it’s fine. It’s your house.

106
00:08:04,417 --> 00:08:05,651
I’ll be okay.

107
00:08:06,652 --> 00:08:07,687
I brought this.

108
00:08:08,354 --> 00:08:10,056
-What's that?
-A sleeping bag.

109
00:08:20,500 --> 00:08:23,135
Mariko is truly incomprehensible.

110
00:08:32,578 --> 00:08:33,613
Hey, stop it.

111
00:08:33,679 --> 00:08:36,649
-What?
-You were staring at me just now, right?

112
00:08:36,716 --> 00:08:38,317
No, no, no, that’s a false accusation.

113
00:08:38,384 --> 00:08:41,554
What? I can’t trust you.
You've been doing this stuff for 25 years.

114
00:08:41,621 --> 00:08:44,991
I will absolutely not cross this line.

115
00:08:45,057 --> 00:08:46,926
I am a man who strictly honors boundaries.

116
00:08:46,993 --> 00:08:48,261
Please rest assured.

117
00:08:54,433 --> 00:08:55,902
What kind of fish do you have?

118
00:08:55,968 --> 00:08:57,270
-What's up?
-Huh?

119
00:08:57,336 --> 00:08:58,905
-What's this? What kind of fish?
-Wait, you're crossing the line.

120
00:08:58,971 --> 00:09:01,040
-I don't have any fish.
-You… You don't?

121
00:09:01,107 --> 00:09:02,942
-They're not very friendly.
-What?

122
00:09:13,686 --> 00:09:14,754
Sota!

123
00:09:15,955 --> 00:09:17,590
I saw on the news
that Hatano is on the run…

124
00:09:17,657 --> 00:09:18,524
Tomoya.

125
00:09:23,729 --> 00:09:24,797
Mariko.

126
00:09:27,633 --> 00:09:29,802
-Thank goodness.
-Tomoya?

127
00:09:31,337 --> 00:09:32,338
Hey.

128
00:09:38,844 --> 00:09:41,013
I'm glad both of you are safe.

129
00:09:42,214 --> 00:09:43,215
Really.

130
00:09:44,850 --> 00:09:45,685
Tomoya?

131
00:09:47,720 --> 00:09:49,188
Ah, sorry, sorry.

132
00:09:51,424 --> 00:09:54,193
Wait, so, does this mean you two are…

133
00:09:55,094 --> 00:09:56,596
-Ah, no, uh…
-Uh…

134
00:09:56,662 --> 00:09:59,065
-It's dangerous, so--
-Ah, got it, got it. I'll leave then.

135
00:09:59,131 --> 00:10:00,666
-Wait, wait…
-See you!

136
00:10:01,233 --> 00:10:03,002
I'm leaving. Don't worry.

137
00:10:19,218 --> 00:10:22,321
-What?
-Quiet!

138
00:10:22,388 --> 00:10:26,792
Yukimura saved you 25 years ago?

139
00:10:27,960 --> 00:10:28,861
Yes.

140
00:10:29,562 --> 00:10:32,365
That must be destiny.

141
00:10:32,431 --> 00:10:33,799
You said there's no such thing as destiny.

142
00:10:33,866 --> 00:10:36,369
-I take it back. There is.
-That was quick.

143
00:10:38,070 --> 00:10:42,041
Still, I feel like it's
pretty different from destiny.

144
00:10:43,509 --> 00:10:46,379
I mean, I haven't actually said
I forgive him or anything.

145
00:10:47,546 --> 00:10:49,882
I shouldn't let my guard down yet.

146
00:10:51,817 --> 00:10:54,887
I don't really get what you mean,
but anyway, Mariko,

147
00:10:55,621 --> 00:10:57,289
you should stop seeing two men at once.

148
00:10:57,356 --> 00:10:58,557
That's bad manners.

149
00:10:59,959 --> 00:11:00,960
What are you talking about?

150
00:11:01,027 --> 00:11:02,828
Your phone's ringing, isn't it?

151
00:11:03,396 --> 00:11:05,798
TAISUKE SAKURA

152
00:11:05,865 --> 00:11:07,767
TAISUKE SAKURA: 13 MISSED CALLS

153
00:11:17,410 --> 00:11:18,244
Whoa…

154
00:11:18,778 --> 00:11:21,380
WHERE ARE YOU?
I SHOULD BE WITH YOU FOR SAFETY.

155
00:11:21,947 --> 00:11:24,483
TAISUKE SAKURA

156
00:11:25,918 --> 00:11:27,586
Excuse me for a second.

157
00:11:39,899 --> 00:11:40,833
Yes, hello?

158
00:11:42,234 --> 00:11:44,637
No, I'm sorry,

159
00:11:44,704 --> 00:11:46,939
I didn’t notice you were calling.

160
00:11:47,006 --> 00:11:49,375
Where did you go yesterday?

161
00:11:50,076 --> 00:11:52,011
It must be scary to be alone, isn't it?

162
00:11:53,245 --> 00:11:56,716
We don't know
when Hatano will attack again.

163
00:12:04,790 --> 00:12:07,193
I'm on Team Yukimura.

164
00:12:07,827 --> 00:12:09,061
Me too.

165
00:12:10,596 --> 00:12:13,566
I mean, what's going on with you two?

166
00:12:15,367 --> 00:12:19,238
I’m probably right on the edge
of a boundary right now.

167
00:12:19,939 --> 00:12:21,640
-A boundary.
-The edge.

168
00:12:21,707 --> 00:12:25,511
You say that,
but the enemy is pressing in hard.

169
00:12:26,445 --> 00:12:28,914
Isn’t that the detective?

170
00:12:28,981 --> 00:12:30,816
Seriously, isn’t he amazing?

171
00:12:30,883 --> 00:12:33,285
I would have given up long ago.

172
00:12:33,853 --> 00:12:35,988
Your enemy is incredibly persistent.

173
00:12:36,622 --> 00:12:38,357
You can't just leave him unchecked.

174
00:12:39,859 --> 00:12:41,727
-No.
-See you.

175
00:12:47,833 --> 00:12:49,902
Yes. Goodbye.

176
00:13:00,946 --> 00:13:02,248
FATHER

177
00:13:06,752 --> 00:13:07,787
Hello?

178
00:13:11,323 --> 00:13:12,391
I'm coming too!

179
00:13:14,794 --> 00:13:18,831
Because I snitched on Yukimura
just to save myself,

180
00:13:19,732 --> 00:13:21,967
I put both of you in danger.

181
00:13:23,002 --> 00:13:26,238
I am truly sorry.

182
00:13:26,305 --> 00:13:28,240
It’s not your fault, Asai.

183
00:13:29,008 --> 00:13:29,842
Right.

184
00:13:31,143 --> 00:13:32,778
It's all my fault.

185
00:13:36,916 --> 00:13:37,850
Asai.

186
00:13:40,452 --> 00:13:41,287
I'm sorry.

187
00:13:43,422 --> 00:13:45,357
Both the kidnapping 25 years ago

188
00:13:46,492 --> 00:13:47,860
and now this.

189
00:13:50,429 --> 00:13:52,097
It's all my fault.

190
00:13:54,400 --> 00:13:55,334
What do you mean?

191
00:13:58,337 --> 00:14:00,072
You were targeted

192
00:14:02,575 --> 00:14:04,376
because you are my daughter.

193
00:14:06,846 --> 00:14:11,517
Hatano and I
were classmates in elementary school.

194
00:14:13,452 --> 00:14:14,353
What?

195
00:14:14,854 --> 00:14:17,122
Right before that kidnapping incident,

196
00:14:18,657 --> 00:14:20,960
there was an elementary school reunion.

197
00:14:21,594 --> 00:14:22,862
And it was there

198
00:14:24,430 --> 00:14:26,198
-that I reunited with Hatano.
-See you!

199
00:14:29,335 --> 00:14:30,336
Gin and tonic.

200
00:14:32,238 --> 00:14:33,672
Hey, Nose.

201
00:14:34,240 --> 00:14:39,078
You couldn't exactly say
Hatano's family was well off.

202
00:14:40,746 --> 00:14:43,182
He always wore the same clothes,

203
00:14:44,416 --> 00:14:46,018
and he was made fun of.

204
00:14:49,655 --> 00:14:51,557
I heard you’ll be
the company president soon?

205
00:14:53,525 --> 00:14:54,393
Yes.

206
00:14:55,194 --> 00:14:58,430
Things are tough at my dad’s factory.

207
00:14:58,497 --> 00:15:03,235
I instantly assumed
he was trying to beg for money.

208
00:15:03,302 --> 00:15:08,307
Sorry, but just because we were classmates
doesn’t mean you can rely on me.

209
00:15:09,108 --> 00:15:12,978
I know things have been rough for you
because of your father, though.

210
00:15:16,615 --> 00:15:18,450
People really don’t change, do they?

211
00:15:20,152 --> 00:15:25,024
I was more pissed off at you than the guys
who actually bullied me back then.

212
00:15:26,325 --> 00:15:28,060
You said to the guys who were bullying me,

213
00:15:28,727 --> 00:15:32,197
"Don't discriminate against someone
because of their family.

214
00:15:32,264 --> 00:15:37,136
Life is determined
by what kind of parents you’re born to."

215
00:15:37,803 --> 00:15:38,804
Right?

216
00:15:39,538 --> 00:15:41,240
Terrible, right?

217
00:15:43,042 --> 00:15:44,743
What’s even more terrible…

218
00:15:48,080 --> 00:15:50,783
is that I didn’t even remember saying it.

219
00:15:54,019 --> 00:15:57,556
"If life changes based on what
kind of parents you are born to…"

220
00:15:59,491 --> 00:16:03,162
Then your daughter
will face the consequences

221
00:16:03,762 --> 00:16:05,531
of being born to you.

222
00:16:09,668 --> 00:16:12,604
Hatano committed his first kidnapping

223
00:16:13,172 --> 00:16:15,441
three days after that reunion.

224
00:16:17,443 --> 00:16:21,780
It is my fault
that everyone was dragged into this.

225
00:16:23,349 --> 00:16:25,317
And yet I tried to hide it.

226
00:16:28,454 --> 00:16:30,222
I am so sorry.

227
00:16:43,002 --> 00:16:46,905
He asked a friend in the police

228
00:16:46,972 --> 00:16:50,542
not to make public the fact
that he had a personal connection

229
00:16:50,609 --> 00:16:51,443
with Hatano.

230
00:16:55,848 --> 00:16:56,715
Thanks.

231
00:16:57,449 --> 00:17:00,119
Both of them were apologetic, Yukimura.

232
00:17:00,919 --> 00:17:04,156
They said they want to apologize to you
in person next time.

233
00:17:06,425 --> 00:17:09,128
Hatano might not even know
what he’s doing anymore.

234
00:17:10,195 --> 00:17:11,397
What?

235
00:17:11,463 --> 00:17:14,767
People can’t live without something
to support them, right?

236
00:17:16,335 --> 00:17:21,240
If Hatano is supporting himself through
resentment or obsession toward someone,

237
00:17:21,306 --> 00:17:23,542
maybe the target could be anyone.

238
00:17:24,610 --> 00:17:27,646
So, why couldn't it just be me?

239
00:17:29,281 --> 00:17:32,084
He might still resent the president,

240
00:17:33,218 --> 00:17:36,955
or maybe he’s just forcibly
clinging to the emotion

241
00:17:37,022 --> 00:17:38,824
of resentment at this point.

242
00:17:41,560 --> 00:17:45,330
-Ah, it’s fine. I’ll do it.
-Oh, thank you.

243
00:17:45,397 --> 00:17:46,231
Here.

244
00:18:08,387 --> 00:18:09,988
Man, I'm hungry now.

245
00:18:10,756 --> 00:18:13,559
-Mariko, do you usually cook at home--
-Hey!

246
00:18:14,093 --> 00:18:16,228
-Stop doing that!
-Doing what?

247
00:18:16,295 --> 00:18:19,231
Every time I put a condiment back,
you turn the label forward like this.

248
00:18:19,298 --> 00:18:22,434
-You’re sneakily straightening them up!
-That's just a habit…

249
00:18:22,501 --> 00:18:24,703
If you want them facing forward,
you could just tell me.

250
00:18:24,770 --> 00:18:26,138
Fixing them behind my back…

251
00:18:26,738 --> 00:18:27,773
-That's just sly.
-No,

252
00:18:27,840 --> 00:18:32,044
-I didn't mean it like that.
-Ah, right! Of course.

253
00:18:32,111 --> 00:18:34,613
You love doing things
behind people's backs, don't you?

254
00:18:34,680 --> 00:18:36,648
-That's right.
-No, no.

255
00:18:36,715 --> 00:18:38,417
Let me ask you this.

256
00:18:38,484 --> 00:18:41,587
Even though you know I was fixing them,

257
00:18:41,653 --> 00:18:43,322
-you still put them down the wrong way?
-Yes.

258
00:18:43,388 --> 00:18:44,656
"Yes"?

259
00:18:46,024 --> 00:18:47,926
What's wrong with that?

260
00:18:48,494 --> 00:18:53,165
Ah, besides, I was planning
to align them all at the end.

261
00:18:53,232 --> 00:18:54,433
You just said "Ah'!"

262
00:18:54,500 --> 00:18:57,336
That's because
you only thought of that just now.

263
00:18:57,402 --> 00:18:59,204
You're being annoying!

264
00:19:00,939 --> 00:19:01,940
Annoying?

265
00:19:03,242 --> 00:19:04,243
You're one to talk.

266
00:19:23,662 --> 00:19:25,264
TAISUKE SAKURA

267
00:19:37,843 --> 00:19:40,913
I’ve been invited
to go to an art exhibition.

268
00:19:41,780 --> 00:19:43,715
-An art exhibition?
-Yes.

269
00:19:44,883 --> 00:19:45,751
To see paintings.

270
00:19:47,653 --> 00:19:50,122
-What do you think?
-What do I think?

271
00:19:51,790 --> 00:19:53,892
Mariko, you aren't even
interested in paintings, right?

272
00:19:54,660 --> 00:19:57,496
What? Why? I am interested.

273
00:19:58,063 --> 00:19:59,531
You're a total liar.

274
00:20:00,032 --> 00:20:02,534
A long time ago, when you went
to an art exhibition with your mother…

275
00:20:09,441 --> 00:20:11,276
Mariko, you don't want to see?

276
00:20:11,343 --> 00:20:12,678
No, it's okay.

277
00:20:13,478 --> 00:20:15,914
You got bored really quickly
and started reading a book, right?

278
00:20:19,017 --> 00:20:20,352
You were watching that too?

279
00:20:23,956 --> 00:20:24,823
Sorry.

280
00:20:27,960 --> 00:20:30,495
My mother loved paintings.

281
00:20:33,398 --> 00:20:35,767
Because my mother loved them,
I wanted to love them too.

282
00:20:39,238 --> 00:20:41,807
Spending time thinking about
the things my mother loved

283
00:20:43,041 --> 00:20:45,410
feels like spending time with her.

284
00:20:51,683 --> 00:20:54,786
I sounded a bit
like you just now, Yukimura.

285
00:21:08,600 --> 00:21:09,768
Is it good?

286
00:21:09,835 --> 00:21:12,070
Oh, sorry, it's very good.

287
00:21:12,804 --> 00:21:13,772
I forgot to say it.

288
00:21:13,839 --> 00:21:14,940
You were just quietly eating.

289
00:21:15,007 --> 00:21:15,941
Sorry.

290
00:21:42,934 --> 00:21:45,103
Yukimura, how much do you know?

291
00:21:47,105 --> 00:21:48,140
What?

292
00:21:49,775 --> 00:21:53,445
My mother was suspected
of having an affair.

293
00:21:55,347 --> 00:21:57,349
I didn't believe it, of course.

294
00:21:59,251 --> 00:22:00,419
There's no way.

295
00:22:02,321 --> 00:22:04,022
My mother wasn't that type of person.

296
00:22:07,893 --> 00:22:09,027
But…

297
00:22:10,362 --> 00:22:13,732
I wonder whose exhibition that was.

298
00:22:14,900 --> 00:22:16,735
Who was she going to meet there?

299
00:22:20,138 --> 00:22:22,874
Maybe there was a side to my mother
that I didn’t know about.

300
00:22:26,545 --> 00:22:30,282
I hated that thought for a long time
and was scared of it,

301
00:22:33,285 --> 00:22:35,921
but now that I’ve reached this age,

302
00:22:36,922 --> 00:22:39,524
I’ve made peace with the fact
that people have different sides.

303
00:22:42,260 --> 00:22:44,096
I think the facet your mother showed you

304
00:22:45,230 --> 00:22:48,533
was also part of her true self.

305
00:22:54,339 --> 00:22:55,474
Yes.

306
00:22:58,910 --> 00:23:00,178
Thank you.

307
00:23:24,803 --> 00:23:26,238
MARIKO WENT TO LOOK
AT PAINTINGS WITH HER MOTHER

308
00:23:51,897 --> 00:23:55,867
-What are you doing?
-No, nothing.

309
00:23:59,438 --> 00:24:03,141
HATANO

310
00:24:03,208 --> 00:24:06,144
I'VE BEEN THINKING ABOUT
HATANO A LOT LATELY

311
00:24:33,939 --> 00:24:36,808
WHY IS THE CAFE CLOSED?

312
00:24:36,875 --> 00:24:40,078
DID SOMETHING HAPPEN?

313
00:25:08,139 --> 00:25:10,342
Hey, kid.

314
00:25:37,035 --> 00:25:39,905
Why don't we settle this already?

315
00:26:07,933 --> 00:26:08,833
Tomoya.

316
00:26:22,314 --> 00:26:23,148
Tomoya.

317
00:26:24,816 --> 00:26:27,152
Stop it. Tomoya, Tomoya.

318
00:26:27,218 --> 00:26:28,787
Stop, Tomoya!

319
00:26:34,392 --> 00:26:36,227
Do you know someone named Mizuki Sagara?

320
00:26:36,795 --> 00:26:37,629
Huh?

321
00:26:38,430 --> 00:26:40,098
Who's that?

322
00:26:45,670 --> 00:26:46,871
You don't remember?

323
00:26:48,239 --> 00:26:50,075
The poor girl whose life ended…

324
00:26:53,111 --> 00:26:54,779
at just nine years old because of you.

325
00:26:55,981 --> 00:26:57,949
You don't remember her?

326
00:27:03,488 --> 00:27:05,724
Tomoya, that's enough. Tomoya.

327
00:27:05,790 --> 00:27:06,992
Tomoya, stop!

328
00:27:07,058 --> 00:27:08,126
-What are you doing?
-Shut up! Get off me!

329
00:27:08,193 --> 00:27:10,295
-Tomoya!
-Die.

330
00:27:10,362 --> 00:27:12,230
-Tomoya!
-Die!

331
00:27:12,297 --> 00:27:13,264
-Hey!
-What are you doing?

332
00:27:14,566 --> 00:27:15,934
Let go of him. Let go!

333
00:27:16,001 --> 00:27:16,901
Hey!

334
00:27:17,836 --> 00:27:19,371
-Don't mess with me!
-Stop!

335
00:27:20,772 --> 00:27:22,440
Don't mess with me!

336
00:27:23,842 --> 00:27:24,843
-Stop.
-Hey!

337
00:27:27,045 --> 00:27:27,879
Stop!

338
00:27:47,165 --> 00:27:50,502
Why am I the only one being arrested?

339
00:27:51,169 --> 00:27:53,438
Man, the world is unfair!

340
00:27:53,505 --> 00:27:55,940
-Shut up already.
-What's wrong with you?

341
00:27:56,875 --> 00:27:57,709
Come on.

342
00:27:58,710 --> 00:28:02,681
Listen, rich people are unfair!

343
00:28:03,782 --> 00:28:05,717
You’re all eyesores.

344
00:28:05,784 --> 00:28:06,751
What's with all of you?

345
00:28:06,818 --> 00:28:08,787
-Hey.
-Calm down, calm down.

346
00:28:08,853 --> 00:28:09,921
What?

347
00:28:13,725 --> 00:28:15,360
You're the eyesore here.

348
00:28:18,630 --> 00:28:20,131
If it weren't for you…

349
00:28:23,668 --> 00:28:24,936
-Sakura!
-That's enough.

350
00:28:25,503 --> 00:28:26,371
Stop it.

351
00:28:44,656 --> 00:28:45,790
Thank you very much.

352
00:28:53,231 --> 00:28:56,701
For now, they said I won't be prosecuted,
but they chewed me out for going too far.

353
00:28:59,137 --> 00:29:00,839
Don't look at me like that.

354
00:29:03,875 --> 00:29:05,610
Hey, there’s a place I want to go.

355
00:29:06,411 --> 00:29:07,512
Mind coming with me?

356
00:29:23,428 --> 00:29:24,662
Coffee's ready.

357
00:29:56,060 --> 00:29:59,364
Ah, here. I know it's important to you.

358
00:30:08,973 --> 00:30:09,874
Tomoya.

359
00:30:12,544 --> 00:30:15,413
How much did you know, and for how long?

360
00:30:20,718 --> 00:30:24,622
At first, it was Mariko.

361
00:30:27,225 --> 00:30:30,028
There were guys spreading rumors
that the daughter of the president

362
00:30:30,094 --> 00:30:31,563
of Nose Cosmetics was one year above us.

363
00:30:32,764 --> 00:30:36,601
Right away, it clicked that she was
the girl from my sister's incident.

364
00:30:40,205 --> 00:30:42,540
"Ah, I was so glad she was alive."

365
00:30:44,843 --> 00:30:47,412
"You survived, and have grown up."

366
00:30:48,112 --> 00:30:49,547
That's what I thought.

367
00:30:49,614 --> 00:30:52,283
Tomoya. Over here!

368
00:31:00,058 --> 00:31:02,961
After that, every time
I saw Mariko on campus,

369
00:31:03,027 --> 00:31:04,229
I couldn’t help but notice her.

370
00:31:06,865 --> 00:31:08,066
But

371
00:31:09,267 --> 00:31:11,636
there was always one guy
who entered my field of vision.

372
00:31:18,643 --> 00:31:20,478
You two didn't seem to be acquaintances.

373
00:31:24,582 --> 00:31:25,750
So I got kind of curious.

374
00:31:32,190 --> 00:31:34,058
-You like that girl, don't you?
-What?

375
00:31:35,126 --> 00:31:36,361
I can tell by looking at you.

376
00:31:37,195 --> 00:31:38,463
No, no, no, that's not…

377
00:31:39,497 --> 00:31:40,732
-You're so easy to read!
-What?

378
00:31:47,839 --> 00:31:48,873
Why?

379
00:31:56,047 --> 00:31:59,417
Why did you have to live your life
carrying so much pain, Tomoya?

380
00:32:02,720 --> 00:32:04,389
You're always cheerful,

381
00:32:05,990 --> 00:32:09,060
kind, thoughtful.

382
00:32:11,195 --> 00:32:13,598
Compared to me,
you're a far better human being.

383
00:32:15,667 --> 00:32:17,135
You're an amazing guy!

384
00:32:18,503 --> 00:32:20,672
You’re such a good guy, Tomoya!

385
00:32:20,738 --> 00:32:22,440
So why did you have to be hurt like this?

386
00:32:26,210 --> 00:32:27,211
Come on.

387
00:32:29,347 --> 00:32:30,315
You’ve…

388
00:32:33,618 --> 00:32:35,653
supported me all this time.

389
00:32:40,291 --> 00:32:42,260
Even though

390
00:32:42,327 --> 00:32:45,797
you found out things that should
have made you abandon me long ago,

391
00:32:47,332 --> 00:32:48,933
you still stayed by my side.

392
00:32:54,172 --> 00:32:57,775
So why have you been
suffering this whole time, Tomoya?

393
00:33:00,178 --> 00:33:01,312
Why?

394
00:33:05,616 --> 00:33:07,652
Why did you have to be
the one to get hurt?

395
00:33:13,191 --> 00:33:14,659
I couldn’t do anything.

396
00:33:18,363 --> 00:33:19,397
You were always by my side…

397
00:33:24,335 --> 00:33:26,204
listening to me, and yet…

398
00:33:27,171 --> 00:33:30,541
And yet I didn't notice a thing.
What was I doing?

399
00:33:31,309 --> 00:33:33,244
I can't forgive myself. I really can't.

400
00:33:36,180 --> 00:33:37,248
I'm sorry, Tomoya.

401
00:33:39,717 --> 00:33:40,718
‎I'm sorry.

402
00:33:44,689 --> 00:33:45,990
‎What's that for?

403
00:33:47,759 --> 00:33:49,093
Why are you apologizing?

404
00:33:58,336 --> 00:34:00,405
It's not like I've lived
with hatred nonstop.

405
00:34:01,806 --> 00:34:04,342
There were times I forgot
about the incident and Hatano.

406
00:34:07,011 --> 00:34:08,179
Or rather…

407
00:34:10,415 --> 00:34:12,984
I learned to live without
constantly remembering it.

408
00:34:16,954 --> 00:34:17,922
But…

409
00:34:19,223 --> 00:34:21,826
when I found out Mariko
and you were attacked…

410
00:34:27,465 --> 00:34:30,501
a rage I’d never felt
before rushed over me.

411
00:34:32,837 --> 00:34:36,174
I figured I'd rather kill him than let
those precious to me be killed again.

412
00:34:43,648 --> 00:34:44,982
Pretty crazy, right?

413
00:34:46,884 --> 00:34:48,953
To think I had such
crazy emotions inside me.

414
00:35:01,432 --> 00:35:03,601
I’m not a decent human being at all.

415
00:35:06,437 --> 00:35:10,241
I was just grinning the whole time
so nobody would notice.

416
00:35:10,308 --> 00:35:12,477
No. That's not true.

417
00:35:14,545 --> 00:35:16,914
I'm sorry, Tomoya.
I couldn't do anything for you.

418
00:35:30,461 --> 00:35:33,531
It's probably because you're like this
that we've been together all this time.

419
00:35:37,201 --> 00:35:39,470
Well, I guess I'm pretty much
the only one who could stay with you.

420
00:35:52,083 --> 00:35:53,818
-Hey!
-What are you doing?

421
00:35:53,885 --> 00:35:55,286
-I'm trying to go home.
-Let's go together.

422
00:35:55,353 --> 00:35:56,254
No, no, no.

423
00:35:57,155 --> 00:35:58,689
Why do you want to go home alone?

424
00:35:58,756 --> 00:35:59,590
I texted you.

425
00:35:59,657 --> 00:36:00,858
-You didn't.
-I did.

426
00:36:35,126 --> 00:36:36,928
Tomoya!

427
00:36:45,770 --> 00:36:49,073
Come on. What were you doing?

428
00:36:50,074 --> 00:36:51,042
Idiot.

429
00:36:54,545 --> 00:36:55,780
Sorry.

430
00:36:58,916 --> 00:36:59,884
I'm sorry.

431
00:37:04,855 --> 00:37:06,257
I'm home…

432
00:37:20,037 --> 00:37:22,907
I'M AT MY FAMILY'S HOUSE
I'LL BE HOME LATE

433
00:37:40,157 --> 00:37:43,995
I wonder whose exhibition that was.

434
00:37:45,062 --> 00:37:47,031
Who was she going to meet there?

435
00:37:59,277 --> 00:38:01,312
-Mariko, you don't want to see?
-July 12th.

436
00:38:01,379 --> 00:38:03,014
‎No, it's okay.

437
00:38:03,080 --> 00:38:06,684
Mariko went to look
at paintings with her mother.

438
00:38:09,353 --> 00:38:14,592
Mariko's mother
was talking happily with a painter,

439
00:38:14,659 --> 00:38:17,061
but Mariko didn’t seem interested.

440
00:38:35,379 --> 00:38:40,551
Today, I saw Mariko's mother
get angry at the florist.

441
00:38:42,820 --> 00:38:45,890
He apologized over and over
for breaking the vase.

442
00:38:46,457 --> 00:38:50,294
She scolded the florist
for not worrying about his own injury.

443
00:38:50,361 --> 00:38:53,064
It made me think she's similar to Mariko.

444
00:38:59,103 --> 00:39:01,205
WORRYING ABOUT HIS OWN INJURY

445
00:39:27,598 --> 00:39:28,599
Mariko.

446
00:39:30,201 --> 00:39:32,536
There's something else
I need to talk with you about.

447
00:39:42,113 --> 00:39:43,581
It's about the secret

448
00:39:44,648 --> 00:39:47,184
between me and Sayuri,
which you asked about.

449
00:39:59,964 --> 00:40:03,901
I’m sorry to bother you at work,
but there's something I'd like to ask.

450
00:40:04,635 --> 00:40:06,003
Wait, you were here the other day?

451
00:40:06,070 --> 00:40:07,872
-Hello!
-Yes.

452
00:40:08,506 --> 00:40:09,440
Twenty-five years ago,

453
00:40:09,507 --> 00:40:12,309
was there someone named
Taisuke Sakura working here?

454
00:40:13,310 --> 00:40:14,512
There was.

455
00:40:15,679 --> 00:40:17,148
Why is everyone asking about that?

456
00:40:17,782 --> 00:40:19,250
I wonder whose exhibition that was.

457
00:40:19,316 --> 00:40:21,018
She was talking happily with a painter.

458
00:40:21,085 --> 00:40:23,020
I saw her get angry at the florist.

459
00:40:23,087 --> 00:40:25,990
She scolded the florist for not worrying
about his own injury.

460
00:40:26,056 --> 00:40:29,593
Is the world really full of coincidences?

461
00:40:29,660 --> 00:40:32,997
I have to protect her from you.

462
00:40:33,898 --> 00:40:39,170
If only you hadn't loved her,
you wouldn't have ended up a criminal.

463
00:40:43,073 --> 00:40:44,141
Thank you very much.

464
00:41:10,868 --> 00:41:13,137
‎KYOKO NOSE

465
00:41:24,815 --> 00:41:25,850
Yes, hello?

466
00:41:28,285 --> 00:41:31,088
Yes. I understand.

467
00:41:33,090 --> 00:41:36,994
I would like to speak with you too.

468
00:41:39,930 --> 00:41:41,065
I'll be waiting.

469
00:41:57,982 --> 00:41:59,917
Stop it already!

470
00:42:05,289 --> 00:42:06,857
I'm at my limit.

471
00:42:10,961 --> 00:42:11,829
You…

472
00:42:14,865 --> 00:42:16,100
It was you.

473
00:42:17,968 --> 00:42:19,603
You kidnapped Mariko.

474
00:42:24,975 --> 00:42:26,210
Why…

475
00:42:28,245 --> 00:42:30,848
Why? Why? Why!?

476
00:42:33,284 --> 00:42:35,019
Why would you say something like that?

477
00:42:43,360 --> 00:42:44,428
Forgive me.

478
00:44:15,219 --> 00:44:18,856
And so, the door containing
all the secrets was opened.

479
00:44:21,125 --> 00:44:22,493
But I could no longer…

480
00:44:24,695 --> 00:44:27,131
protect Mariko.

481
00:44:28,932 --> 00:44:30,334
Don't mess with me!

482
00:44:30,968 --> 00:44:33,370
‎NEXT TIME…

483
00:44:37,941 --> 00:44:38,876
‎Subtitle translation by: Maslin Friedman
